  "caveats": [
    "Centring uses the held-out labels, so R2_centred is an oracle-offset bound, not a deployable score. The claim it supports is about within-metal ordering.",
    "The identifiable set uses ligand_canonical, the same key as UP-10/UP-11. Keying on ligand_main_fragment (the Morgan input) gives a much larger set and is reported as a sensitivity, but it conflates 'seen this ligand' with 'seen this scaffold'.",
    "Re has zero identifiable rows: no (ligand, cell) unit measured under Re is also measured under another metal, so nothing about Re transfers.",
    "Per-metal centred R2 on 177-406 rows has a wide interval; the secondary gate counts metals, it does not test them individually.",
    "Rows are the deduplicated table (21,045), so a ligand measured many times in one paper counts once per (ligand, cell, metal) group; n is not independent."
  ]
